  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Palantir Usg has $1.2B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, across 50 awards with an average award size of $23.7M. Obligations are up 59.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, accounting for $1.1B of obligations in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of State with $18M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $12.1M. Historical obligations show growth from $67.6M in FY21 to $1.2B in FY26, with interim totals of $198M in FY22, $151M in FY23, $288M in FY24, and $745M in FY25. Custom Computer Programming Services is the largest NAICS market with $1B in obligations in FY2026 to date, with Software Publishers showing $124M and a separate Software Publishers entry at $236K. Other identified markets include Other Management Consulting Services at $27.1M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $247K.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Palantir Usg's largest federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.1B in FY2026 to date. The Department of State is the second-largest buyer with $18M, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $12.1M and the U.S. International Development Finance Corporation with $8.1M. Those four agencies together account for the bulk of the reported FY2026 obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services account for Palantir Usg's federal obligations?",
        "body": "Custom Computer Programming Services is the largest market with $1B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Software Publishers appears with $124M and again with $236K in separate entries, Other Management Consulting Services shows $27.1M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences shows $247K. The average award size across obligations is $23.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
